Making process

Seedance 2.5 Draft -> 1080P

@Image 1 defines the heroine's identity, short dark wavy hair, slender long-limbed proportions, and outfit: oversized tan V-neck tee, voluminous tan balloon pants with ribbed cuffs, cream sneakers. Treat all panels as one person. Do not use its white background, panel layout, or headless crops. @Image 2 defines the world and visual style: soft painterly stylized 3D illustration, towering cumulus clouds, blue sky, floating stacked shanty-town towers with dangling cables. Do not use its static pose or framing as the first frame. Keep this painterly stylized medium throughout. No photorealistic skin. Preserve facial identity and proportions while allowing natural expression changes, breathing, and head movement.  Setup: a single ultra-thin line is stretched across open sky between two floating towers, high above the clouds. The line is almost invisible, so she appears to stand on air. She is the only person.  [0–3s] Wide establishing shot, slow crane up from below a cloud bank. She stands on the line mid-span, arms out, balancing, pants swaying in wind. Calm, focused gaze ahead.  [3–6s] Side-profile tracking dolly moving with her. She takes three quick steps, plants both hands on the line, and performs a front walkover: legs sweep over, one foot lands, then the other, weight recovers over the line. Brief speed ramp to slow motion at the top of the arc, then back to normal speed.  [6–9s] Top-down bird's-eye view straight down past her body to the clouds far below. She launches a no-hands front aerial; the balloon pants billow open around her legs. On landing her body wobbles; a short dolly-zoom vertigo stretches the drop below.  [9–12s] Extreme close-up on her sneaker pressing the line, which flexes slightly. Rack focus along the line: sunlight catches it once and a spider-silk glint travels along its length, then fades, and the line is invisible again. Her arms correct the balance; she exhales, steadies.  [12–16s] Dutch-angle FPV orbit circling her a full 360°. She spins a controlled pirouette on one foot into an arabesque, arms extended, the floating towers sliding past behind her. Her expression shifts from tension to a confident small smile.  [16–20s] Extreme low worm's-eye angle. She performs a final front tuck flip, lands cleanly with both feet on the line, knees absorbing, arms opening wide. The camera pulls back and rises to a wide shot; she holds the final pose, chin lifted, looking toward the distant clouds.  Physics: every jump shows push-off, hand or foot contact on the line, and balance recovery. The line sags slightly under her weight and rebounds. Hair and fabric follow her motion and the wind. Danger is felt through wobbles and the drop below, but she never falls.  Audio: high-altitude wind, fabric flapping <whoosh>, soft line creak <creak> on landings, a faint shimmer <ting> at the glint. No music, no dialogue, no subtitles, no text.

